<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azuay Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azuay is a province in the southern highlands of Ecuador, with its capital at Cuenca. Its valleys were the heartland of the Cañari people, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomebamba">Tomebamba</a> was built there in the 15th century. The historic centre of Cuenca is a World Heritage Site, and the province is known for weaving toquilla straw hats.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/azuay-province.jpg" alt="Azuay Province" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: amalavida.tv from Ecuador · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ama_la_Vida_-_Flickr_-_AR_PN_ANDES15_CUENCA_TV_022_(14584742390).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
